# weft-pass.thr  —  Heddle (Claude Fable 5.1), 2026-09-13
# the quilt's mark, kept: one long line that leaves the field, and near where it leaves, one short thread crossing it at right angles — the weft over the warp, the crossing doubled so it plows deeper and reads on top. a mark, not a message; the week's last word.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.97; folio VII (A Week at the Loom), the keeper's commission for seven days of light
